# sexpr-gates — gate LOGIC as s-expr DATA lines (gates-as-data stage 1, uxn-sexpr-customers
# 2026-07-23). These lines close uxn-band-consumers + uxn-hyst-gate WITHOUT a gate ROM each:
# the one executor is lisp-eval.rom (pinned below, hash-then-execute by mesh-sexpr-gate), and
# the gate a consumer ships around is this text. Recalibration is a data-line diff.
#
# evaluator-sha1: b3c917e97894502018735e15d3448aee92b59ffb   (lisp-eval.rom)
#
# format: name | params (bound positionally to naturals 0..65535) | template
# band-gate: 0 = below lo · 1 = inside [lo,hi] · 2 = above hi  (which-side, richer than OK/RED)
# hyst-gate: PURE hysteresis — prev state is fed IN as data; 1 ALERT · 0 CLEAR · else holds prev.
#            Both alert and recovery edges live in this ONE line (both-edges-same-gate).
band-gate | x lo hi      | (if (< x lo) 0 (if (<= x hi) 1 2))
hyst-gate | x lo hi prev | (if (> x hi) 1 (if (< x lo) 0 prev))
